@startuml connection_setup
!theme cyborg
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
title What runs inside one connection setup, and under which deadline?
participant COMMUNICATION
participant WIFI
participant "DNS resolver" as DNS
participant "pool.ntp.org" as NTP
participant "HTTPS server" as Server
note over COMMUNICATION
 One monotonic deadline for the whole setup:
 Idle preparation 10 s (P26), delivery attempt 3 s (P13).
 Waits of at most 200 ms only let Start be seen; they never extend it.
end note
COMMUNICATION -> WIFI : start time synchronization (SNTP)
WIFI -> DNS : resolve pool.ntp.org (IPv4)
WIFI -> NTP : one SNTP request, UDP/123; no resend
NTP --> WIFI : reply
WIFI --> COMMUNICATION : normalized sample (reject leap 3, stratum outside 1-15,\nuncertainty above 100 ms)
COMMUNICATION -> WIFI : apply clock: new UTC/monotonic anchor
COMMUNICATION -> COMMUNICATION : server certificate valid at the new UTC time?\nno: fail before any ClientHello
COMMUNICATION -> WIFI : start secure connection
WIFI -> DNS : resolve server endpoint
WIFI -> Server : TCP connect, TLS 1.3 handshake (ClientHello first)
Server --> WIFI : verified server: certificate, name, validity
WIFI --> COMMUNICATION : verified connection, retained as reuse candidate
note over COMMUNICATION, Server
 Any failure (DNS, SNTP, clock, TCP, TLS, deadline) fails the whole setup: Idle retries after 60 s,
 delivery follows P13. No separate SNTP schedule, refresh timer or expiry: a reused connection runs no SNTP.
 Cancellation has its own 1 s stop bound (P23) outside this deadline.
end note
@enduml
